  "question": {
    "text": "If $f(x)=\\frac{e^x}{1+e^x}, l_1=\\int_{f(-a)}^{f(a)} x g\\{x(1-x)\\} d x$ and $I_2=\\int_{f(-a)}^{f(a)} g\\{x(1-x)\\} d x$ then the value of $\\frac{l_2}{l_1}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "UAJT6",
      "text": "\n2\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "EuvM5",
      "text": "\n$-3$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2tb3s",
      "text": "\n$-1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qsNeW",
      "text": "\n1",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$f(-a)+f(a)=1$\n$I_1=\\int_{f(-a)}^{f(a)} x g\\{x(1-x)\\} d x=\\int_{f(-a)}^{f(a)}(1-x) g\\{x(1-x)\\} d x \\quad\\left(\\because \\int_a^b f(x) d x=\\int_a^b f(a+b-x) d x\\right)$\n$2 I_1=\\int_{f(-a)}^{f(a)} g\\{x(1-x)\\} d x=I_2 \\Rightarrow I_2 / I_1=2$.",
    "image": null
  },
